{"reference":"2 Chronicles 31","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":31,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Renewed All-Israel Horizon","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents Hezekiah’s restoration of temple worship within a wider renewal that included both Judah and northern Israel. The associated Passover gathering in Jerusalem is described in terms of prayer, healing, joy, and Levitical service, giving the renewal an all-Israel horizon.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 31:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_031_f92ab783a16f7da1adf5505b"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}